the omicron variant causing a big spike  in cases hospitals throughout the state  are struggling to keep up with staffing  demands a nevada hospital association  report explains staffing levels are at a  critical stage joe muller spoke to some  hospital staff about what is actually  going on he's live outside sunrise  hospital with more joe  christian we have seen the long lines of  cars with people trying to get tested  for coven 19. meantime hospitals like  sunrise here are dealing with a spike in  patients a new report shows just how  impacted hospitals are  it's spreading like  wildfire mountain view hospital nurse  nicole taylor says times are getting  tough nurses are calling out sick at an  astronomical rate that leaves the nurses  who aren't sick  to essentially pick up the slack an  update from the nevada hospital  association this week shows staffing  remains at crisis levels at hospitals  throughout the valley a representative  from mountain view sunrise and southern  hills hospitals tells me they have all  seen an increase of 105 percent over the  last two weeks in copen 19 patients  nurses and health care workers are  feeling  exhausted i also spoke to stephen murta  the chief medical officer from sunrise  hospital and medical center we too are  feeling the same  staffing challenges he says they are  making staffing adjustments to make sure  they can take care of patients they are  utilizing the nurse and then  and bringing on a cna which is a  certified nursing assistant  or a patient care technician and have  them work in teams so that they that one  nurse can manage more murder and many  others say people are showing up to  hospitals looking for copin 19 tests and  that is putting a strain on operations  er is here for you in an acute care  emergency but if you have minor  illnesses or you're looking for a  testing site please go to the southern  nevada health district  national nurses united plans to hold a  demonstration shedding the light on the  snapping problems nationwide here  locally they plan to hold a  demonstration tomorrow at 8 a.m outside  of mountain view hospital reporting live  joe muller live local now  joe thank you for that well in regards  to tomorrow's demonstration a  representative from mountain view tells  us no one cares more for our colleagues  than they do they say it is  disappointing that the labor union  leadership doesn't recognize the  valuable contributions of all colleagues  who are working to help patients
 

